A||||3||fiero56||car cover?||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||06-08-2001||06:36 PM||||I'm leaving my folks place and moving out to do the apartment thing, and the apartment community I'm moving to hasn't finished my garage(they just poured the cement Friday). I don't want to park my Fiero in the hot sun for several weeks with no shade(hitting high 80s around here). I'm thinking about a car cover to slow down the paint fade, and keep the interior from warping. Are car covers very good at keeping interior temps of the car lower? Are they very damaging to paint? Pros/cons?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroLisa||06-08-2001||06:48 PM||||I use a car cover every once in a while, definitely not all the time, but then again I have new-er paint ( a couple mos. old). A car cover shouldn't scratch paint, but Chris Moore had a nice car cover on his convertible and it scratched up the paint, even though the paint is 10 yrs old. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||06-08-2001||07:02 PM||||The thing is I have two Fieros. One daily driver, and one backup. I will be parking my Formula for at least the month, so it won't be a daily removal/putting on cover. More of a semi-permanant cover.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||06-08-2001||07:13 PM||||Check out the CoverCraft website and search/read the fabrics sections. There is a table that shows all of them and they rate their properties for handling snow, rain, sun, dents, heat, etc. etc. I bought the Technalon 4 (evolution4 before) which is very good for heat. Their best for "shade" is UMBRELLA or something like that. Key item you want in a car cover is UV protection. That's what fades paint. A good car cover used on a clean car should not scratch the paint. I have been using mine everyday at work since I painted my car last March. No scratches and car is cooler when I open it. Mine cost $99 at PepBoys. Fiero Store sells the same but for $170+s/h cause it has Fiero mirror pockets & tighter fit. IMOO I wouldn't pay the premium. The normal one fits very nice. Hope this helps you a little bit.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
